<https://w3id.org/gelmat/> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionIRI> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/1.1.0> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#imports> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#imports> <https://w3id.org/polymat/> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/> <http://omv.ontoware.org/2005/05/ontology#designedForOntologyTask> "knowledge representation in sol-gel materials synthesis, characterisation, and material properties" .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/> <http://omv.ontoware.org/2005/05/ontology#usedOntologyEngineeringTool> "https://www.isibang.ac.in/ns/mod/index.html#Protege" .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/abstract> "Gelmat is an ontology for sol-gel materials. It extends the Polymat domain ontology with classes for sol-gel synthesis processes, gel characterisation methods, drying routes, laboratory equipment, process parameters, and material properties. It enables semantic description and formal documentation of sol-gel and aerogel research workflows, covering silica, organosilica, organic, carbon, and composite sol-gel derived materials." .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/author> "Antoni Dudij, Institute for Frontier Materials on Earth and in Space, German Aerospace Center (DLR), Cologne, Germany" .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/author> "Barbara Milow (https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6350-7728), Institute for Frontier Materials on Earth and in Space, German Aerospace Center (DLR), Cologne, Germany" .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/author> "Prakul Pandit (https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1343-3046), Institute for Frontier Materials on Earth and in Space, German Aerospace Center (DLR), Cologne, Germany" .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/bibliographicCitation> "Pandit, P., Dudij, A., & Milow, B. (2026). Gelmat: An Ontology for Sol-Gel Materials (Version 1.1.0). German Aerospace Center (DLR). https://w3id.org/gelmat/" .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-03-12"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-NC-4.0.html> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-09-14"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Gelmat: An Ontology for Sol-Gel Materials" .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/> <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespacePrefix> "gmat" .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/> <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespaceUri> "https://w3id.org/gelmat/" .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Gelmat is an ontology for sol-gel materials. It extends the Polymat ontology (Dembska, Held, Schindler; DLR/Hereon) with classes for sol-gel synthesis routes, gel types, surface modification, drying methods, characterisation methods, process parameters, and material properties. Covers all major sol-gel derived material classes including silica, organosilica, organic, carbon, and composite aerogels." .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Gelmat" .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "1.1.0" .
