# https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasCanonicalUnit
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasCanonicalUnit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasCanonicalUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has canonical unit"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasCanonicalUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Links a quantity class to the canonical (recommended) OM-2 unit of measure in which instances of that quantity are conventionally expressed. Machine-readable counterpart to the unit named in the class definition."@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasCanonicalUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/Unit> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasStepOrder
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasStepOrder> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasStepOrder> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has step order"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasStepOrder> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An integer indicating the canonical execution order of a sub-process within a synthesis workflow (1 = first step). Used to provide SPARQL-queryable ordering of BFO parthood sub-steps that are otherwise unordered."@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasStepOrder> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#positiveInteger> .
