# https://w3id.org/polymat/isParameterOf
<https://w3id.org/polymat/isParameterOf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/polymat/isParameterOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/polymat/Feature> .
<https://w3id.org/polymat/isParameterOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000003> .
<https://w3id.org/polymat/isParameterOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a quantity or process feature (temperature, duration, pH) to the process it characterises. Preferred over obo:RO_0000052 when the bearer is a process rather than a material entity. Range is BFO occurrent (BFO_0000003) rather than BFO process (BFO_0000015) because process steps are pmat:Method (under pmat:Procedure, a prov:Entity) while BFO_0000015 maps to prov:Activity, which PROV-O declares disjoint from prov:Entity — a BFO_0000015 range would make every class with an isParameterOf existential unsatisfiable"@en .
<https://w3id.org/polymat/isParameterOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is parameter of"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/polymat/usesOperatingSystem
<https://w3id.org/polymat/usesOperatingSystem> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/polymat/usesOperatingSystem> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/polymat/Software> .
<https://w3id.org/polymat/usesOperatingSystem> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/polymat/OperatingSystem> .
<https://w3id.org/polymat/usesOperatingSystem> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "uses the low-level software which handles the interface to peripheral hardware, schedules tasks, allocates storage, and presents a default interface to the user when no application program is running\r\n(http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C47908)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/polymat/usesOperatingSystem> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "uses operating system"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/polymat/usesRuntimeEnvironment
<https://w3id.org/polymat/usesRuntimeEnvironment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/polymat/usesRuntimeEnvironment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/polymat/Software> .
<https://w3id.org/polymat/usesRuntimeEnvironment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/polymat/RuntimeEnvironment> .
<https://w3id.org/polymat/usesRuntimeEnvironment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "uses a sub-system that exists both in the computer where a program is created, as well as in the computers where the program is intended to be run. \r\n(https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Runtime_system)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/polymat/usesRuntimeEnvironment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "uses runtime environment"@en .
