<https://w3id.org/gelmat/APDAerogelSynthesis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An aerogel synthesis route using ambient pressure drying (APD). Requires a surface modification step (typically silylation with TMCS or HMDS) between solvent exchange and drying to prevent capillary collapse during the drying step"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/APDAerogelSynthesis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Ambient pressure drying aerogel synthesis"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/APDAerogelSynthesis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "APD synthesis"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/APDAerogelSynthesis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An aerogel synthesis route in which the wet gel is dried at ambient pressure after mandatory surface silylation; avoids high-pressure equipment of supercritical drying by preventing capillary collapse through hydrophobic surface modification"@en .
