<https://w3id.org/gelmat/AcidCatalysis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Sol-gel gelation under acid-catalytic conditions (pH < 7). Promotes fast hydrolysis and slower condensation, yielding weakly branched, polymeric gel structures with smaller pores"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/AcidCatalysis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Acid-catalysed gelation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/AcidCatalysis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Acid catalysis"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/AcidCatalysis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Gelation performed at pH below 7, where protonation of alkoxide leaving groups accelerates hydrolysis relative to condensation, yielding weakly branched, polymeric gel networks with small pores"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/AcidCatalysisPathway
