<https://w3id.org/gelmat/AcidCatalysisPathway> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A gelation pathway realised through acid catalysis: pre-hydrolysis at low pH followed by slow condensation, producing weakly branched polymeric network gels with small, homogeneous pores."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/AcidCatalyst
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/AcidCatalyst> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/AcidCatalyst> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/Acid> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/AcidCatalyst> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A Bronsted or Lewis acid used specifically as a catalyst in sol-gel hydrolysis and condensation reactions (e.g. HCl, HNO3, acetic acid, oxalic acid). Convenience class typed by chemical nature; the primary way to state that a substance functions as a catalyst in a given step is the role pattern: step gmat:usesSubstance substance, substance prov:hadRole [a pmat:Catalyst]"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/AcidCatalyst> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Acid catalyst"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/AcidCatalyst> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Acid catalytic agent"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/AcidCatalyst> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An acid employed as a catalyst; in sol-gel processing, promotes hydrolysis of alkoxide precursors under acidic conditions"@en .
# 
