<https://w3id.org/gelmat/AerogelSynthesis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The complete process of synthesizing aerogels from precursor materials through sol-gel chemistry followed by a drying step. Only sol formation, gelation, and drying are asserted as required parts (owl:someValuesFrom); aging, solvent exchange, and surface modification are common but optional steps that many published syntheses omit, so they carry no existential restriction here — asserting them would make every extracted synthesis without such a step inconsistent under OWL reasoning"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/AerogelSynthesis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Aerogel synthesis"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/AerogelSynthesis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The complete multi-step process of producing an aerogel from precursor substances, comprising at minimum sol formation, gelation, and a drying step that preserves pore structure; aging, solvent exchange, and surface modification are frequent optional steps"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/Aging
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Aging> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Aging> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/CreationProcess> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Aging> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Post-gelation maturation process where the gel network strengthens through continued condensation reactions and Ostwald ripening. Typically performed by keeping the wet gel immersed in solvent at elevated temperature"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Aging> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Aging"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Aging> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Post-gelation maturation in which the wet gel is kept immersed in solvent at elevated temperature to strengthen the network via continued condensation reactions, Ostwald ripening, and syneresis, reducing later shrinkage during drying"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Aging> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasStepOrder> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#positiveInteger> .
