# https://w3id.org/gelmat/AmbientPressureDrying
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/AmbientPressureDrying> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/AmbientPressureDrying> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/polymat/Drying> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/AmbientPressureDrying> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Drying method performed at atmospheric pressure, typically requiring surface modification to prevent capillary collapse"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/AmbientPressureDrying> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Ambient pressure drying"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/AmbientPressureDrying> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "APD"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/AmbientPressureDrying> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Evaporative drying"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/AmbientPressureDrying> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A drying method performed at atmospheric pressure in which capillary collapse is prevented by prior surface silylation of the gel, allowing the hydrophobic network to spring back after compression and recover its pore volume"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/Ambigel
