# https://w3id.org/gelmat/ArrheniusConstant
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ArrheniusConstant> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ArrheniusConstant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/Quantity> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ArrheniusConstant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The pre-exponential factor (A) in the Arrhenius equation k = A·exp(−Ea/RT), representing the frequency of molecular collisions with correct orientation. Units match the rate constant (e.g., s⁻¹ for first-order reactions)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ArrheniusConstant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Arrhenius pre-exponential factor"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ArrheniusConstant> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Arrhenius constant"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ArrheniusConstant> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Frequency factor"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ArrheniusConstant> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A quantity representing the pre-exponential factor A in the Arrhenius equation, reflecting the frequency of correctly oriented molecular collisions"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ArrheniusConstant> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasCanonicalUnit> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/reciprocalSecond-Time> .
