# https://w3id.org/gelmat/Base
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Base> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Base> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_24431> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Base> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A Bronsted base capable of accepting a proton. Bases serve as catalysts for condensation reactions in sol-gel processing (e.g. ammonium hydroxide, ammonium fluoride, sodium hydroxide)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Base> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Base"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Base> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A chemical entity capable of accepting a proton (Bronsted base) or donating an electron pair (Lewis base)"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/BaseCatalysis
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/BaseCatalysis> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/BaseCatalysis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/Gelation> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/BaseCatalysis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid60 .
_:genid60 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/Base> .
_:genid60 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/usesSubstance> .
_:genid60 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/BaseCatalysis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Sol-gel gelation under basic conditions (pH > 7). Promotes fast condensation and slower hydrolysis, yielding highly branched, colloidal cluster networks with larger pore sizes"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/BaseCatalysis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Base-catalysed gelation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/BaseCatalysis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Base catalysis"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/BaseCatalysis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Gelation performed at pH above 7, where hydroxide ions catalyse condensation faster than hydrolysis, yielding highly branched, colloidal cluster-cluster aggregation networks with larger pore sizes"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/BaseCatalysisPathway
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/BaseCatalysisPathway> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/BaseCatalysisPathway> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/GelationPathway> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/BaseCatalysisPathway> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid61 .
_:genid61 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/BaseCatalysis> .
_:genid61 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/realisedAs> .
_:genid61 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/BaseCatalysisPathway> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Base Catalysis Pathway"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/BaseCatalysisPathway> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A gelation pathway realised through base catalysis: fast condensation relative to hydrolysis at high pH, producing highly branched colloidal aggregation networks with larger pore sizes."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/BaseCatalyst
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/BaseCatalyst> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/BaseCatalyst> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/Base> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/BaseCatalyst> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A class of chemical substances that provide basic conditions or catalyze base-mediated reactions (e.g., deprotonation, nucleophilic activation) in a process. Convenience class typed by chemical nature; the primary way to state that a substance functions as a catalyst in a given step is the role pattern: step gmat:usesSubstance substance, substance prov:hadRole [a pmat:Catalyst]"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/BaseCatalyst> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Base Catalyst"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/BaseCatalyst> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A base employed as a catalyst; in sol-gel processing, promotes condensation reactions under basic conditions"@en .
