# https://w3id.org/gelmat/CarbonAerogel
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CarbonAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CarbonAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/Aerogel> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CarbonAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/OrganicAerogel> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CarbonAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An aerogel with a purely carbonaceous framework, produced by pyrolysis of an organic precursor aerogel (e.g. resorcinol-formaldehyde) above 700 °C in inert atmosphere. The pyrolysis destroys all organic bonds, leaving an electrically conductive elemental carbon network. Not subclassed under OrganicAerogel — carbon aerogels contain no C-H bonds"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CarbonAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Carbon aerogel"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CarbonAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Activated carbon aerogel"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CarbonAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A pyrolysed aerogel whose solid framework consists of elemental (sp² or sp³ hybridised) carbon, distinct from organic aerogels which retain organic polymer backbones"@en .
