# https://w3id.org/gelmat/CompressiveModulus
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CompressiveModulus> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CompressiveModulus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/ModulusOfElasticity> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CompressiveModulus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The ratio of compressive stress to compressive strain in the elastic region of the stress-strain curve, expressed in kPa or MPa. For aerogels this reflects network stiffness and cross-linking density"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CompressiveModulus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Compressive modulus"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CompressiveModulus> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Young's modulus (compression)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CompressiveModulus> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The elastic modulus measured under uniaxial compression, equal to the slope of the linear region of the compressive stress-strain curve"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CompressiveModulus> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasCanonicalUnit> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/pascal> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/CompressiveStrength
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CompressiveStrength> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CompressiveStrength> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/CompressiveStress> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CompressiveStrength> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The maximum compressive stress a material can sustain before fracture, yielding, or excessive deformation. A critical mechanical property for structural and load-bearing aerogel applications"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CompressiveStrength> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Compressive strength"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CompressiveStrength> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A material property quantity representing the maximum compressive stress a material can withstand before failure; expressed as an om:Measure with unit kPa or MPa."@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CompressiveStrength> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasCanonicalUnit> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/pascal> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/Condensation
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Condensation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Condensation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/CreationProcess> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Condensation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid62 .
_:genid62 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/Silanol> .
_:genid62 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/usesSubstance> .
_:genid62 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Condensation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Reaction between silanol groups (Si-OH + HO-Si -> Si-O-Si + H2O) or between silanol and alkoxy groups forming siloxane bonds that build the three-dimensional gel network"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Condensation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Condensation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Condensation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Formation of siloxane (Si-O-Si) network bonds by reaction of silanol intermediates, releasing water or alcohol as by-products"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/ContactAngle
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ContactAngle> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ContactAngle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/Quantity> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ContactAngle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The angle at which a liquid-vapor interface meets a solid surface, quantifying wettability. Key metric for hydrophobic aerogels (contact angle > 90 degrees) and superhydrophobic aerogels (contact angle > 150 degrees)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ContactAngle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Contact angle"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ContactAngle> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A material property quantity representing the angle between a liquid droplet interface and a solid surface, used to quantify hydrophobicity; expressed as an om:Measure with unit degrees. Values above 90° indicate hydrophobic surfaces."@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ContactAngle> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasCanonicalUnit> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/radian> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/Cooling
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Cooling> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
