# https://w3id.org/gelmat/CorrelationLength
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CorrelationLength> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CorrelationLength> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/Length> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CorrelationLength> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The upper cutoff length ξ of fractal scaling in an aerogel network, corresponding to the characteristic cluster (blob) size above which the material appears homogeneous. Obtained from the crossover (knee) in a SAXS/SANS curve; typically a few to tens of nanometres"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CorrelationLength> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Correlation length"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CorrelationLength> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Cluster size"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CorrelationLength> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Fractal correlation length"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CorrelationLength> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The correlation length ξ marking the upper length-scale cutoff of fractal self-similarity in a gel network (the characteristic cluster/blob size), determined from the low-q crossover of a scattering curve"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CorrelationLength> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasCanonicalUnit> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/metre> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/Cracking
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Cracking> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Cracking> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/AerogelDefect> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Cracking> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The defect state of one or more cracks being present in the aerogel structure. Typically results from capillary stress or rapid pressure/temperature changes during drying — but this class denotes the persisting crack feature, not the crack-formation event."@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Cracking> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Crack"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Cracking> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Cracking"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Cracking> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An aerogel defect consisting of one or more fracture discontinuities in the solid network of the material"@en .
