# https://w3id.org/gelmat/Crosslinker
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Crosslinker> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Crosslinker> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_24431> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Crosslinker> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A chemical agent that forms bonds between polymer chains to create network structures. Convenience class typed by chemical nature; the primary way to state the function in a given step is the role pattern: step gmat:usesSubstance substance, substance prov:hadRole [a gmat:CrosslinkerRole]"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Crosslinker> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Crosslinker"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Crosslinker> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A chemical agent that forms covalent or physical bonds between polymer chains, producing a three-dimensional network structure"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/CrosslinkerRole
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CrosslinkerRole> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CrosslinkerRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/polymat/Role> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CrosslinkerRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The role of a substance that forms bonds between polymer chains or particles in a given step; distinct from the convenience substance class gmat:Crosslinker, which types substances by chemical nature"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CrosslinkerRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Crosslinker role"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/CrosslinkerRole> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A role borne by a substance that bridges polymer chains or colloidal particles into a network during a synthesis step"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/Cryogel
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Cryogel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Cryogel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/Gel> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Cryogel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A dried gel obtained by freeze drying (lyophilisation) of a wet gel; ice crystal growth typically leaves a more macroporous, often lamellar structure than supercritical drying"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Cryogel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Cryogel"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Cryogel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A dried gel produced by freezing the pore liquid and removing it by sublimation (freeze drying)"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/Curing
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Curing> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Curing> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalTreatment> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Curing> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Moderate-temperature treatment that completes cross-linking or imidisation of a polymer network (e.g. thermal imidisation of poly(amic acid), post-curing of RF gels)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Curing> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Curing"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Curing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A thermal treatment that completes the cross-linking reactions of a polymer or hybrid network"@en .
