# https://w3id.org/gelmat/Density
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Density> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Density> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/Quantity> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Density> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The mass per unit volume of a material. Canonical unit: kg/m3 (SI); the lab convention g/cm3 (= 1000 kg/m3) is also common. Bulk density is typically 1-500 kg/m3 (0.001-0.5 g/cm3); skeletal density (determined by He pycnometry) is typically 1800-2200 kg/m3 (1.8-2.2 g/cm3) for silica"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Density> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Density"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Density> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The ratio of the mass of a material to its volume; for aerogels the bulk density captures the contribution of both the solid skeleton and the gas-filled pore space"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Density> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasCanonicalUnit> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/kilogramPerCubicmetre> .
