<https://w3id.org/gelmat/DryingControlChemicalAdditive> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Chemical additives (DCCA) used to reduce capillary stress and prevent cracking during ambient pressure drying. Convenience class typed by chemical nature; the primary way to state the function in a given step is the role pattern: step gmat:usesSubstance substance, substance prov:hadRole [a gmat:DryingControlAdditiveRole]"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/DryingControlChemicalAdditive> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Drying control chemical additive"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/DryingControlChemicalAdditive> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "DCCA"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/DryingControlChemicalAdditive> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A chemical additive incorporated into a sol to reduce capillary stress and prevent cracking during drying"@en .
