# https://w3id.org/gelmat/MassFractalDimension
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/MassFractalDimension> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/MassFractalDimension> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/FractalDimension> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/MassFractalDimension> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceFractalDimension> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/MassFractalDimension> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The fractal dimension Dm describing the power-law scaling of network mass with length scale in the fractal (low-q) region of the scattering curve, I(q) ∝ q^(−Dm). Values 1.7-2.4 are typical for silica aerogels; lower values indicate more open, chain-like structures"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/MassFractalDimension> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Mass fractal dimension"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/MassFractalDimension> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Dm"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/MassFractalDimension> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Mass fractal dimension"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/MassFractalDimension> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The mass fractal dimension (1 ≤ Dm ≤ 3) obtained from the slope of the fractal regime of a SAXS/SANS curve, describing how network mass scales with observation length"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/MassFractalDimension> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasCanonicalUnit> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/one> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/MassFraction
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/MassFraction> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/MassFraction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/Quantity> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/MassFraction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The mass of a component divided by the total mass of the mixture or composite, expressed as a fraction or wt%. Covers fibre loading, solid content, silica content, and similar compositional quantities"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/MassFraction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Mass fraction"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/MassFraction> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Weight fraction"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/MassFraction> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "wt%"@en .
