# https://w3id.org/gelmat/OrganicAerogel
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/OrganicAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/OrganicAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/Aerogel> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/OrganicAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An aerogel in which the solid framework is composed of organic macromolecules (polymers, biopolymers) rather than inorganic networks or elemental carbon"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/OrganicAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Organic aerogel"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/OrganicAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An aerogel whose solid framework consists of an organic polymer network (e.g. resorcinol-formaldehyde, polyimide, cellulose). Distinguished from carbon aerogels by retention of organic functional groups and from inorganic aerogels by the absence of metal oxide or silica frameworks"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/OrganicPrecursor
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/OrganicPrecursor> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/OrganicPrecursor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/Precursor> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/OrganicPrecursor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A small organic molecule that polycondenses into an organic gel network (resorcinol-formaldehyde and related chemistries); the parent chemistry of organic and, after pyrolysis, carbon aerogels"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/OrganicPrecursor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Organic precursor"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/OrganicPrecursor> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An organic monomer that forms an organic polymer network by polycondensation in sol-gel synthesis"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/OrganosilicaAerogel
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/OrganosilicaAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/OrganosilicaAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/HybridAerogel> .
