# https://w3id.org/gelmat/Oven
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Oven> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Oven> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/Dryer> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Oven> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A thermally insulated chamber used for drying, heating, or thermal treatment of materials at controlled temperatures. In aerogel processing, ovens are used for ambient pressure drying and post-treatment heat curing"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Oven> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Oven"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Oven> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A dryer consisting of a thermally insulated chamber for drying, heating, or thermal treatment at controlled temperature"@en .
