# https://w3id.org/gelmat/PHAdjuster
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PHAdjuster> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PHAdjuster> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_24431> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PHAdjuster> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A substance used to control pH during gelation or processing, such as acids or bases"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PHAdjuster> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "pH adjuster"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PHAdjuster> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A substance added to control the pH of a mixture during gelation or processing"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/PHCondition
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PHCondition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PHCondition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/ProcessParameter> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PHCondition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The pH level maintained during a sol-gel process step (sol formation, gelation, aging). Acid conditions (pH 1-5) favour hydrolysis; base conditions (pH 7-10) favour condensation. pH is controlled by addition of acid or base catalysts. As a ProcessParameter this class is an om:Quantity, so the preferred value pattern is om:hasValue pointing to a dimensionless om:Measure (see gmat:PHValue); gmat:hasPHValue remains available as a datatype shortcut"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PHCondition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "pH condition"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PHCondition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A process parameter specifying the hydrogen ion concentration of the reaction medium, expressed on a scale of 0-14, that governs the relative rates of hydrolysis and condensation in sol-gel synthesis"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/PHValue
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PHValue> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PHValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/Quantity> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PHValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The pH of a solution or reaction medium as a dimensionless quantity (0-14). Preferred over the datatype shortcut gmat:hasPHValue when the value should participate in the om:Quantity/om:Measure pattern; a gmat:PHCondition process parameter carries its magnitude as a PHValue-style dimensionless om:Measure"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PHValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "pH value"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PHValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "pH"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PHValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A dimensionless quantity representing the negative decadic logarithm of the hydrogen ion activity of a solution"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PHValue> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasCanonicalUnit> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/one> .
# 
