# https://w3id.org/gelmat/PoissonRatio
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PoissonRatio> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PoissonRatio> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/Quantity> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PoissonRatio> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The negative ratio of transverse strain to axial strain under uniaxial load; a dimensionless elastic constant. Reported for aerogels to characterise their compressible, low-Poisson network (often 0.1-0.2)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PoissonRatio> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Poisson ratio"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PoissonRatio> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Poisson's ratio"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PoissonRatio> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The dimensionless ratio of transverse contraction strain to longitudinal extension strain in the direction of an applied uniaxial load"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PoissonRatio> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasCanonicalUnit> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/one> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/PolyimideAerogel
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PolyimideAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PolyimideAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/PolymerAerogel> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PolyimideAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An organic aerogel based on polyimide polymer chains"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PolyimideAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Polyimide aerogel"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PolyimideAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A polymer aerogel whose network is formed from polyimide chains"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/PolymerAerogel
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PolymerAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PolymerAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/Aerogel> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PolymerAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An aerogel composed of organic polymer networks, such as resorcinol-formaldehyde, polyurethane, or polyimide aerogels"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PolymerAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Polymer aerogel"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PolymerAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An aerogel whose solid network is composed of organic polymer chains"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/PolymerPrecursor
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PolymerPrecursor> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PolymerPrecursor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/Precursor> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PolymerPrecursor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A monomer or oligomer that forms a synthetic polymer aerogel network by step-growth chemistry: dianhydrides and diamines (polyimide), isocyanates and polyols (polyurethane/polyurea)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PolymerPrecursor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Polymer precursor"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PolymerPrecursor> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A monomer or oligomer that forms a synthetic polymer network in polymer aerogel synthesis"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/Polyol
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Polyol> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Polyol> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/PolymerPrecursor> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Polyol> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A polyfunctional alcohol that reacts with isocyanates to form the polyurethane network of polyurethane aerogels"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Polyol> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Polyol"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Polyol> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A polyfunctional alcohol monomer that forms polyurethane networks with isocyanates"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/PolyurethaneAerogel
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PolyurethaneAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PolyurethaneAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/PolymerAerogel> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PolyurethaneAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An aerogel based on a polyurethane polymer network formed by the reaction of polyisocyanates with polyols"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PolyurethaneAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Polyurethane aerogel"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PolyurethaneAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A polymer aerogel whose network is formed by the reaction of polyisocyanates with polyols"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/PoreSizeDistribution
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PoreSizeDistribution> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PoreSizeDistribution> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/Quantity> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PoreSizeDistribution> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A statistical description of the range and frequency of pore sizes within a porous material, typically determined by BJH analysis or mercury intrusion porosimetry. Aerogels predominantly feature mesopores (2-50 nm)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PoreSizeDistribution> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Pore size distribution"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PoreSizeDistribution> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A material property describing the statistical distribution of pore sizes within a porous material, typically characterised by BJH analysis of N₂ adsorption isotherms."@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PoreSizeDistribution> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasCanonicalUnit> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/metre> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/PoreVolume
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PoreVolume> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PoreVolume> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/Quantity> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PoreVolume> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The volume of open pores per unit mass of a porous material, as reported in the literature from N2 physisorption (total pore volume at p/p0 ~ 0.99) or mercury intrusion; conventionally given in cm3/g (= 0.001 m3/kg). A specific (mass-normalised) volume, hence placed directly under om:Quantity rather than om:Volume, with canonical unit m3/kg"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PoreVolume> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Pore volume"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PoreVolume> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Specific pore volume"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PoreVolume> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Total pore volume"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PoreVolume> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A quantity representing the total volume of open pores per unit mass of a porous material"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PoreVolume> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasCanonicalUnit> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/cubicMetrePerKilogram> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/PorodExponent
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PorodExponent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PorodExponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/Quantity> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PorodExponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The power-law exponent P of the scattering intensity, I(q) ∝ q^(−P), in the high-q region. Directly read from the scattering slope: 1 ≤ P ≤ 3 indicates a mass fractal (P = Dm), while 3 < P ≤ 4 indicates a surface fractal (P = 6 − Ds), with P = 4 for a smooth (Porod) interface"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PorodExponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Porod exponent"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PorodExponent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Power-law exponent"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PorodExponent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Scattering exponent"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PorodExponent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The dimensionless power-law exponent of small-angle scattering intensity versus q, from which the mass fractal (P = Dm) or surface fractal (P = 6 − Ds) dimension is derived"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PorodExponent> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasCanonicalUnit> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/one> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/Porosity
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Porosity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Porosity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/Quantity> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Porosity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The ratio of void volume to total volume in a porous material, expressed as a fraction or percentage. Aerogels typically exhibit porosity > 90%, which directly impacts their thermal, acoustic, and mechanical properties"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Porosity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Porosity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Porosity> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A material property quantity representing the fraction of void space in a material relative to its total volume; expressed as an om:Measure with unit fraction (0–1) or percent."@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Porosity> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasCanonicalUnit> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/one> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/PorosityMeasurement
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PorosityMeasurement> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PorosityMeasurement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/polymat/Analysis> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PorosityMeasurement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Measurement of pore volume, pore size distribution, and surface area, typically using BET or BJH methods"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PorosityMeasurement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Porosity measurement"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PorosityMeasurement> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An analysis that determines pore volume, pore size distribution, or related textural properties of a porous material"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/Precursor
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Precursor> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Precursor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_24431> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Precursor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A chemical entity that is chemically converted into the solid network of a gel during sol-gel synthesis. Grouped by material family: silica, metal oxide, organic, polymer, and biopolymer precursors. The function in a specific step is additionally stated through the role pattern (prov:hadRole some gmat:PrecursorRole)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Precursor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Precursor"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Precursor> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A chemical entity that reacts to form the solid network of a gel in sol-gel synthesis"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/PrecursorRole
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PrecursorRole> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PrecursorRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/polymat/Role> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PrecursorRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The role of a substance that is chemically converted into the solid network of the gel (e.g. TEOS in a silica synthesis, resorcinol and formaldehyde in an RF synthesis)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PrecursorRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Precursor role"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PrecursorRole> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A role borne by a substance that serves as the network-forming reactant of a sol-gel synthesis step"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/PressurePlate
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PressurePlate> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PressurePlate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/polymat/Instrument> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PressurePlate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A device to apply and distribute a precise, uniform compressive load."@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PressurePlate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Pressure Plate"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PressurePlate> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An instrument that applies and distributes a precise, uniform compressive load to a specimen"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/PressureProfile
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PressureProfile> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PressureProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/ProcessParameter> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PressureProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Pressure conditions including set points, ramp rates, and hold times during a process"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PressureProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Pressure profile"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PressureProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A process parameter representing the pressure conditions of a process, including set points, ramp rates, and hold times"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/PressureVessel
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PressureVessel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PressureVessel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/polymat/Equipment> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PressureVessel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Container designed to hold gases or liquids at pressure different from ambient"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PressureVessel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Pressure vessel"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/PressureVessel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Equipment consisting of a container designed to hold gases or liquids at a pressure substantially different from ambient"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/Pressurization
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Pressurization> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Pressurization> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/polymat/SamplePreparation> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Pressurization> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Controlled increase of pressure during supercritical drying to bring the drying fluid above its critical point, typically performed at controlled ramp rate"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Pressurization> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Pressurization"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Pressurization> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A sample preparation step in which pressure is increased in a controlled manner, in supercritical drying bringing the drying fluid above its critical point"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/ProcessParameter
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ProcessParameter> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ProcessParameter> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ProcessParameter> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/Quantity> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ProcessParameter> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A quality (in the BFO sense) that characterises the material inputs or setup of a synthesis process — e.g. a molar or volume ratio of reagents, a pH condition, or a stirring rate. Modelled as a quality that inheres in an independent continuant (typically the reacting mixture / sol), carrying its numeric magnitude via an om:Measure. Achieved, per-run values (not plan prescriptions). Also a subclass of om:Quantity (itself under pmat:Feature), so that process parameters can carry values via om:hasValue and satisfy the pmat:Feature domain of pmat:isParameterOf."@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ProcessParameter> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Process parameter"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ProcessParameter> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A quality inhering in an independent continuant that characterises the material inputs or setup of a synthesis process, recording an achieved per-run value"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/Pycnometer
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Pycnometer> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Pycnometer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/polymat/Instrument> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Pycnometer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Device for measuring volume and density of materials, typically using helium displacement"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Pycnometer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Pycnometer"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Pycnometer> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Helium pycnometer"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Pycnometer> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An instrument that measures the volume and density of a material, typically by gas displacement"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/Pyrolysis
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Pyrolysis> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Pyrolysis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalTreatment> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Pyrolysis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Thermal decomposition of an organic aerogel in inert atmosphere (N2, Ar), typically 600-1100 degC, converting it into a carbon aerogel"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Pyrolysis> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Pyrolysis"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Pyrolysis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Carbonisation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Pyrolysis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Carbonization"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Pyrolysis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A thermal treatment in inert atmosphere that decomposes an organic network into carbon; the route from organic to carbon aerogels"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/RamanSpectroscopy
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/RamanSpectroscopy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/RamanSpectroscopy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/polymat/Analysis> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/RamanSpectroscopy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Raman scattering spectroscopy; for carbon aerogels the D/G band ratio quantifies graphitisation, for oxides it identifies phases"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/RamanSpectroscopy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Raman spectroscopy"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/RamanSpectroscopy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An analysis that records inelastic (Raman) light scattering to characterise molecular and lattice vibrations"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/RatioValue
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/RatioValue> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/RatioValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/Measure> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/RatioValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A value node representing the numerical proportion between substances in a ratio; a dimensionless om:Measure pointed to by a ProcessParameter quality, not a quality itself. Single-valued ratios carry om:hasNumericalValue (xsd:double, unit om:one; two-part ratio a:b = a/b) for numeric querying, alongside the display string in gmat:hasRatioString. Multi-component ratios (e.g. '1:10:4:4') are represented by the string only."@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/RatioValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Ratio Value"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/RatioValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A dimensionless measure holding the numerical proportion between substances in a ratio, referenced by a process parameter quality"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/RawData
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/RawData> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
