# https://w3id.org/gelmat/Shrinkage
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Shrinkage> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Shrinkage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/Quantity> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Shrinkage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The relative dimensional change (linear or volumetric) of a gel during the drying process, expressed as a fraction or percentage. High shrinkage indicates capillary-force-driven pore collapse, common in ambient pressure drying"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Shrinkage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Shrinkage"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Shrinkage> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A material property quantity representing the linear dimensional change of a gel or aerogel during processing (drying, aging) relative to the original gel dimension; expressed as an om:Measure with unit percent."@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Shrinkage> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasCanonicalUnit> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/one> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/Silanol
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Silanol> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Silanol> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_24431> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Silanol> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A silicon hydroxide species (Si-OH) formed as an intermediate during hydrolysis of silicon alkoxide precursors. Silanols undergo condensation to form siloxane (Si-O-Si) bonds and build the gel network"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Silanol> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Silanol"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Silanol> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An intermediate species containing a silicon-bound hydroxyl group (Si-OH), the key reactive monomer formed by hydrolysis of silicon alkoxides in sol-gel processing"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilicaAerogel
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilicaAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilicaAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/InorganicAerogel> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilicaAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An aerogel with a pure silicon dioxide (SiO₂) backbone, typically produced from tetraethoxysilane (TEOS) or tetramethylorthosilicate (TMOS) via the sol-gel process followed by supercritical drying"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilicaAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Silica aerogel"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilicaAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "SiO₂ aerogel"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilicaAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <http://emmo.info/emmo#EMMO_4207e895> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilicaAerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An inorganic aerogel in which the solid network consists predominantly of amorphous SiO₂, giving low density (0.003–0.35 g/cm³), high surface area (> 500 m²/g), and low thermal conductivity"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilicaPrecursor
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilicaPrecursor> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilicaPrecursor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/Precursor> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilicaPrecursor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A precursor that yields a silica (SiO2) or organosilica network, comprising silicon alkoxides (TEOS, TMOS, MTMS, ...) and silicates (sodium silicate / water glass)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilicaPrecursor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Silica precursor"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilicaPrecursor> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A precursor whose hydrolysis and condensation yield a silica or organosilica network"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilicatePrecursor
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilicatePrecursor> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilicatePrecursor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilicaPrecursor> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilicatePrecursor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An inorganic silicate salt used as a low-cost silica source, typically requiring an ion exchange or acid neutralisation step to remove the alkali cations before or during gelation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilicatePrecursor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Silicate precursor"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilicatePrecursor> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An inorganic silicate used as a silica source in the water-glass route to silica gels"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/SiliconAlkoxidePrecursor
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SiliconAlkoxidePrecursor> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SiliconAlkoxidePrecursor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/OrganosiliconCompound> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SiliconAlkoxidePrecursor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilicaPrecursor> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SiliconAlkoxidePrecursor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A subclass of organosilicon compounds with silicon bound to alkoxy groups (Si–OR); commonly employed as sol–gel precursors for silica networks"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SiliconAlkoxidePrecursor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Silicon alkoxide precursor"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SiliconAlkoxidePrecursor> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A silicon compound bearing hydrolysable alkoxy groups (Si-OR), employed as a sol-gel precursor for silica or organosilica networks"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilylationAgent
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilylationAgent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilylationAgent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_24431> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilylationAgent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A reactive organosilicon compound used to replace silanol surface groups with alkylsilyl groups, rendering the gel surface hydrophobic. Applied during surface modification before ambient pressure drying. Convenience class typed by chemical nature; the primary way to state the function in a given step is the role pattern: step gmat:usesSubstance substance, substance prov:hadRole [a gmat:SilylationAgentRole]"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilylationAgent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Silylation agent"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilylationAgent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Silylating agent"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilylationAgent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reactive organosilicon compound that replaces surface silanol groups with alkylsilyl groups, rendering a gel surface hydrophobic"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilylationAgentRole
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilylationAgentRole> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilylationAgentRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/polymat/Role> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilylationAgentRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The role of a substance that silylates surface silanol groups during a surface modification step; distinct from the convenience substance class gmat:SilylationAgent"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilylationAgentRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Silylation agent role"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilylationAgentRole> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A role borne by a substance that replaces surface silanol groups with alkylsilyl groups during surface modification"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/Sintering
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Sintering> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
