<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SolFormation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SolFormation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/CreationProcess> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SolFormation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid72 .
_:genid72 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/Condensation> .
_:genid72 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051> .
_:genid72 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SolFormation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid73 .
_:genid73 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/Hydrolysis> .
_:genid73 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051> .
_:genid73 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SolFormation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Process of creating a colloidal suspension (sol) by mixing precursors, solvents, and catalysts before gelation. Comprises hydrolysis of alkoxide groups and condensation of silanol intermediates"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SolFormation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Sol formation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SolFormation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The first stage of sol-gel synthesis in which precursor molecules undergo hydrolysis and initial condensation to form a stable colloidal suspension (sol) of nanoscale particles or oligomers in a solvent"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SolFormation> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasStepOrder> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#positiveInteger> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/SolGelPolymerisation
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SolGelPolymerisation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SolGelPolymerisation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/GelationPathway> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SolGelPolymerisation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A gelation pathway involving the polymerization of precursors via sol-gel chemistry"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SolGelPolymerisation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Sol-gel polymerisation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SolGelPolymerisation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A gelation pathway in which the network forms by polymerisation of precursors via hydrolysis and condensation reactions"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/SolGelTransition
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SolGelTransition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SolGelTransition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/CreationProcess> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SolGelTransition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The gel point event at which the sol loses fluidity and transitions to a solid gel network due to percolation of the condensing silica network. Characterised by a sharp increase in viscosity and loss of flow. Placed under gmat:CreationProcess (not under gmat:Gelation, whose usesSubstance existentials would be wrongly inherited by an instantaneous event) so that it is visible to anything that enumerates synthesis steps; the containment in gelation is expressed by gmat:Gelation asserting BFO_0000051 (has part) some SolGelTransition"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SolGelTransition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Sol-gel transition"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SolGelTransition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Gel point"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SolGelTransition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Gelation point"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SolGelTransition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The critical event (gel point) at which percolation of the condensing network spans the reaction volume, converting the flowable sol into a solid gel; marked by divergence of viscosity and loss of steady-state flow"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/SolidStateNMR
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SolidStateNMR> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SolidStateNMR> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/polymat/Analysis> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SolidStateNMR> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Solid-state NMR spectroscopy (29Si, 13C, 27Al); 29Si Q/T-species ratios quantify network connectivity (gmat:NetworkConnectivity) and condensation degree; performed on a pmat:NMRSpectrometer"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SolidStateNMR> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Solid-state NMR spectroscopy"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SolidStateNMR> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "ssNMR"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SolidStateNMR> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An analysis that records nuclear magnetic resonance spectra of solid samples, typically under magic-angle spinning"@en .
