# https://w3id.org/gelmat/SpringbackFailure
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SpringbackFailure> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SpringbackFailure> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/AerogelDefect> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SpringbackFailure> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Incomplete recovery of pore volume after capillary compression during ambient pressure drying; the gel does not fully spring back to its wet-gel dimensions due to insufficient surface silylation or network weakness"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SpringbackFailure> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Springback failure"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SpringbackFailure> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An aerogel defect in which the gel network fails to recover its original pore volume after capillary compression during ambient pressure drying, due to insufficient hydrophobisation or network weakness, yielding higher density and lower surface area than expected"@en .
