# https://w3id.org/gelmat/StructuralCollapse
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/StructuralCollapse> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/StructuralCollapse> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/AerogelDefect> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/StructuralCollapse> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The defect state of a collapsed or densified aerogel network, typically caused by capillary forces during improper drying. Denotes the persisting collapsed-structure feature of the material, not the collapse event."@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/StructuralCollapse> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Collapsed structure"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/StructuralCollapse> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Structural collapse"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/StructuralCollapse> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An aerogel defect consisting of a collapsed or densified region of the solid network in which the original porous structure is lost"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalCO2
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalCO2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalCO2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalFluid> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalCO2> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalEthanol> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalDryer
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalDryer> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalDryer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/Dryer> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalDryer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Specialized equipment for supercritical drying that heats and pressurizes fluid (typically CO2) above its critical point to extract solvents from gel materials"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalDryer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Supercritical dryer"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalDryer> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Autoclave"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalDryer> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A dryer that heats and pressurises a fluid above its critical point to extract pore solvent from a gel without capillary stress"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalDrying
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalDrying> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalDrying> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/polymat/Drying> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalDrying> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Drying method using supercritical fluid (typically CO2) to remove solvent from porous materials while preserving the nanoscale structure by avoiding capillary forces"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalDrying> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Supercritical drying"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalDrying> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A drying method in which the pore liquid is brought above its critical temperature and pressure before venting to gas phase, eliminating the liquid-vapour interface and thus capillary stress, preserving the aerogel network"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalEthanol
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalEthanol> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalEthanol> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalFluid> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalEthanol> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Ethanol in supercritical state (above 241°C and 61.4 bar), alternative to CO2 for aerogel drying"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalEthanol> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Supercritical ethanol"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalEthanol> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Ethanol in the supercritical state, used as a high-temperature alternative drying medium in supercritical drying of gels"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalEthanol> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#relatedMatch> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_16236> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalFluid
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalFluid> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalFluid> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/polymat/Substance> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalFluid> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A substance at temperature and pressure above its critical point, exhibiting properties between gas and liquid phases"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalFluid> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Supercritical fluid"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalFluid> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A substance held at a temperature and pressure above its critical point, exhibiting properties intermediate between those of a gas and a liquid"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalFluidRole
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalFluidRole> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalFluidRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/polymat/Role> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalFluidRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The role of a substance used in its supercritical state as the extraction medium of a supercritical drying step (typically CO2 or ethanol)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalFluidRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Supercritical fluid role"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SupercriticalFluidRole> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A role borne by a substance that serves as the supercritical extraction medium in a supercritical drying step"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceArea
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceArea> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceArea> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/Quantity> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceArea> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The specific surface area (BET) of a porous material in m2/g, measured by N2 physisorption and analysis of the adsorption isotherm using the Brunauer-Emmett-Teller model. Aerogels typically exhibit 200-1000 m2/g"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceArea> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Surface area"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceArea> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "BET surface area"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceArea> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Specific surface area"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceArea> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The total internal and external surface area of a porous material per unit mass, determined by BET N2 physisorption; the primary indicator of aerogel texture and catalytic or adsorption capacity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceArea> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasCanonicalUnit> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/squareMetrePerGram> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceFractalDimension
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceFractalDimension> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceFractalDimension> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/FractalDimension> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceFractalDimension> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The fractal dimension Ds describing the roughness/self-similarity of the solid-pore interface, obtained from the Porod region of the scattering curve, I(q) ∝ q^(−(6−Ds)). Values 2 ≤ Ds < 3, where Ds = 2 denotes a smooth surface and values toward 3 denote an increasingly rough, space-filling interface"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceFractalDimension> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Surface fractal dimension"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceFractalDimension> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Ds"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceFractalDimension> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The surface fractal dimension (2 ≤ Ds ≤ 3) obtained from the Porod region of a SAXS/SANS curve, quantifying the roughness of the solid-pore interface"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceFractalDimension> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasCanonicalUnit> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/one> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceModification
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceModification> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceModification> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/polymat/SamplePreparation> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceModification> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Chemical treatment to alter aerogel surface properties, such as hydrophobization or functionalization"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceModification> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Surface modification"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceModification> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Chemical treatment of the internal pore surfaces of a wet gel to alter surface chemistry, typically to introduce hydrophobic groups that prevent capillary collapse during ambient pressure drying"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceSilylation
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceSilylation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceSilylation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceModification> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceSilylation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> _:genid75 .
_:genid75 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/SilylationAgent> .
_:genid75 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasSilylationAgent> .
_:genid75 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceSilylation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Chemical modification of wet gel surface Si-OH groups by reaction with a silylating agent (TMCS, HMDS) to replace surface hydroxyls with hydrophobic alkylsilyl groups. Essential pre-treatment before ambient pressure drying to prevent capillary collapse"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceSilylation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Surface silylation"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceSilylation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Hydrophobic surface modification"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceSilylation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "TMCS treatment"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfaceSilylation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A surface modification step in which surface silanol groups (Si-OH) react with a chlorosilane or silazane reagent (e.g. TMCS, HMDS) to install hydrophobic trialkylsilyl groups, enabling ambient pressure drying"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/Surfactant
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Surfactant> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Surfactant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_24431> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Surfactant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A surface-active agent used to stabilize emulsions or modify interfacial properties in synthesis. Convenience class typed by chemical nature; the primary way to state the function in a given step is the role pattern: step gmat:usesSubstance substance, substance prov:hadRole [a gmat:SurfactantRole]"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Surfactant> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Surfactant"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Surfactant> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A surface-active agent that lowers interfacial tension, used to stabilise emulsions or modify interfacial properties during synthesis"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfactantRole
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfactantRole> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfactantRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/polymat/Role> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfactantRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The role of a substance acting as a surface-active agent (emulsion stabiliser, pore templating agent) in a given step; distinct from the convenience substance class gmat:Surfactant"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfactantRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Surfactant role"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SurfactantRole> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A role borne by a substance that lowers interfacial tension or templates porosity during a synthesis step"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/SynthesisProtocol
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SynthesisProtocol> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SynthesisProtocol> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000031> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SynthesisProtocol> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A plan specification (recipe/protocol) that prescribes how a sol-gel synthesis is to be carried out. As a generically dependent continuant it is the reusable, copyable information artifact that a concrete synthesis process (an occurrent) realises. Distinguishes the recipe from any individual run of it."@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SynthesisProtocol> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Synthesis protocol"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SynthesisProtocol> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A generically dependent continuant that is an information artifact prescribing the ordered activities, materials, and conditions for carrying out a sol-gel synthesis; realised by one or more concrete synthesis processes."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/SyringePump
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SyringePump> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SyringePump> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/polymat/Pump> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SyringePump> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/VacuumPump> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SyringePump> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A precision fluid delivery device that uses a motor-driven plunger to dispense exact volumes at controlled flow rates. Used in aerogel synthesis for controlled addition of reagents or for supercritical fluid delivery"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SyringePump> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Syringe Pump"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/SyringePump> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A pump that dispenses precise fluid volumes at controlled flow rates by means of a motor-driven plunger"@en .
