# https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalConductivity
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalConductivity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalConductivity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/ThermalConductivity> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalConductivity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The property of a material to conduct heat, defined as the rate of heat flow through a unit thickness per unit area per unit temperature difference. For aerogels, low thermal conductivity is a key performance metric, with values typically in the range 0.012-0.025 W/(m*K)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalConductivity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Thermal conductivity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalConductivity> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A material property quantity representing the rate of heat transfer through a material; expressed as an om:Measure with unit W/(m·K). Lower values indicate better thermal insulation."@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalConductivity> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasCanonicalUnit> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/wattPerMetreKelvin> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalConductivityTesting
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalConductivityTesting> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalConductivityTesting> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/polymat/Analysis> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalConductivityTesting> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Measurement of heat transfer properties through aerogel material"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalConductivityTesting> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Thermal conductivity testing"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalConductivityTesting> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An analysis that measures the heat transport properties of a material"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalDiffusivity
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalDiffusivity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalDiffusivity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/ThermalDiffusivity> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalDiffusivity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The rate at which heat diffuses through a material, equal to thermal conductivity divided by the product of density and specific heat capacity, expressed in m^2/s. Very low for aerogels, reflecting their insulating behaviour"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalDiffusivity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Thermal diffusivity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalDiffusivity> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A material property quantity representing the rate of thermal diffusion through a material (thermal conductivity / (density × specific heat capacity)); expressed as an om:Measure with unit m²/s"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalDiffusivity> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasCanonicalUnit> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/squareMetrePerSecond-Time> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalExpansionCoefficient
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalExpansionCoefficient> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalExpansionCoefficient> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/Quantity> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalExpansionCoefficient> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The fractional change in length (linear) per unit change in temperature at constant pressure, expressed in K^-1. OM-2 defines no dedicated class, so this quantity is placed directly under om:Quantity with a reciprocal-kelvin canonical unit"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalExpansionCoefficient> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Thermal expansion coefficient"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalExpansionCoefficient> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "CTE"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalExpansionCoefficient> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Coefficient of thermal expansion"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalExpansionCoefficient> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Linear thermal expansion coefficient"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalExpansionCoefficient> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A material property quantity representing the linear coefficient of thermal expansion, i.e. the relative change in a material's length per unit temperature change at constant pressure; expressed as an om:Measure with unit K⁻¹"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/ThermalExpansionCoefficient> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasCanonicalUnit> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/reciprocalKelvin> .
