<https://w3id.org/gelmat/WaterToSilicaRatio> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "H2O:Si ratio"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/WaterToSilicaRatio> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "r-ratio"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/WaterToSilicaRatio> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The molar ratio r = [H2O]/[Si] of water to silicon alkoxide precursor; governs the completeness of hydrolysis. Stoichiometric full hydrolysis of TEOS requires r = 4; r < 4 yields partially hydrolysed species; r >> 4 produces fully hydrolysed, more condensed networks"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/WetGel
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/WetGel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/WetGel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/Gel> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/WetGel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A gel containing liquid within its porous network structure, formed after gelation and before drying. The liquid phase determines the specific type (hydrogel if water, alcogel if alcohol)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/WetGel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Wet gel"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/WetGel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A gel whose pore network is filled with a liquid phase, existing after gelation and before drying"@en .
