# https://w3id.org/gelmat/Xerogel
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Xerogel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Xerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/Gel> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Xerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A dried gel with a collapsed or partially collapsed pore structure, formed when a wet gel is dried under ambient conditions causing capillary forces to shrink the network"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Xerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Xerogel"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/Xerogel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A dried gel formed when a wet gel is dried under ambient conditions; capillary forces during liquid evaporation partially or fully collapse the pore network, resulting in a denser material than the corresponding aerogel"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/gelmat/YoungsModulus
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/YoungsModulus> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/YoungsModulus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/ModulusOfElasticity> .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/YoungsModulus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The ratio of tensile (or uniaxial) stress to axial strain in the linear-elastic region of the stress-strain curve, expressed in Pa. Characterises the intrinsic stiffness of the aerogel solid network; typically 10^4-10^7 Pa for silica aerogels"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/YoungsModulus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Young's modulus"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/YoungsModulus> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Elastic modulus"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/YoungsModulus> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Modulus of elasticity"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/YoungsModulus> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The elastic modulus relating uniaxial stress to axial strain in the linear-elastic regime; equal to the slope of the initial linear portion of the stress-strain curve"@en .
<https://w3id.org/gelmat/YoungsModulus> <https://w3id.org/gelmat/hasCanonicalUnit> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/pascal> .
