# https://w3id.org/polymat/Permeability-Diffusion
<https://w3id.org/polymat/Permeability-Diffusion> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/polymat/Permeability-Diffusion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/Quantity> .
<https://w3id.org/polymat/Permeability-Diffusion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Describes the penetration of a permeate (a fluid such as a liquid, gas, or vapor) through a solid (such as a membrane); it is directly proportional the materials' diffusion coefficient and inversly proportional to the concentration or pressure gradient of the permeate\r\n\r\nP = V･d / (A･t･p) = D / p\r\nP = permeability (diffusion)\r\nV = Volume of the permeate [m³]\r\nd = thickness of the membrane [m]\r\nA = area of the membrane [m²]\r\nt = time of diffusion [s]\r\np = pressure difference [atm]\r\nD = Diffusion coefficient = diffusivity [m²/s]\r\n\r\nThe SI unit of the permeability (diffusion) is m²/(s･atm); the proportional unit E-10･cm²/(s･Torr) is commonly called  Barrer."@en .
<https://w3id.org/polymat/Permeability-Diffusion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Permeability (diffusion)"@en .
