<https://w3id.org/polymat/TimeLag> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A method commonly used to characterize gas separation membranes. It allows the determination of diffusion, permeability, and solubility coefficients from a single dynamic gas permeation experiment; for this experiment, a homogeneous membrane is exposed to a step increase in pressure at one side of the membrane (feed side) and the feed pressure remains constant, while the other side (permeate side) of the membrane remains under vacuum; the diffusion and permeability coefficients are then determined from the resulting permeate pressure-time curve; the solubility coefficient is the permeability coefficient divided by the diffusion coefficient\r\n(https://doi.org/10.1016/j.memsci.2020.118715)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/polymat/TimeLag> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Time lag"@en .
