<https://w3id.org/polymat/TransmissionElectronMicroscope> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A piece of equipment which is used to produce an enlarged image of an electron transparent specimen using a finely focused (<10 nm diameter) electron beam with an acceleration voltage of 50–150 kV under vacuum; the energies and intensities of the transmitted electrons are measured\r\n(http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHMO_0001099)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/polymat/TransmissionElectronMicroscope> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A type of microscope that uses magnetic lenses to transmit a beam of electrons through a thin sample; the electrons are then focused on a fluorescent screen or another detector to form an enlarged image\r\n(https://www.photonics.com/EDU/transmission_electron_microscope_TEM/d7604)"@en .
<https://w3id.org/polymat/TransmissionElectronMicroscope> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An electron microscope that transmits a beam of electrons through a finely sliced section of a specimen and creates an image of the sample based on its effect on the phase of the electrons that pass through\r\n(http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C78813)"@en .
